<title>USA: U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. wheat major net sales activity in the week ended Sept 26 reported by exporters for the following purchasing countries, in tonnes:</p>
<p>Net Sales:    1996/97		   1997/98</p>
<p> Yemen	  120,000		    Nil</p>
<p> South Africa  64,600</p>
<p> Jordan	  50,000</p>
<p> Trinidad	50,000</p>
<p> Panama	  42,300</p>
<p> Philippines   39,600</p>
<p> Mexico	  39,300</p>
<p> Brazil	 -28,300</p>
<p> South Korea  -20,900</p>
<p> Peru	   -15,900</p>
<p>Net sales of 585,100 tonnes were 58 percent above the previous week and 30 percent above the four-week average.</p>
<p>Exports of 951,800 tonnes were 23 percent above the four-week average.</p>
<p>Primary Export Destinations: Egypt, Philippines, Pakistan, Turkey, Japan, and Israel.</p>
</text>
